  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Relistor (methylnaltrexone bromide) Criteria Version 2; effective 2019-11-20.",
    "Available forms: 8mg/0.4ml syringe, 12mg/0.6ml kit, 12mg/0.6ml syringe, 12mg/0.6ml vial, 150mg tablet.",
    "FDA indications (notes only): tablet for OIC in adults with chronic non-cancer pain; injection for OIC in adults with chronic non-cancer pain and OIC in adults with advanced illness receiving palliative care when response to laxative therapy has been insufficient.",
    "All five approval requirements are encoded; denials mirror age, indication, opioid duration, obstruction exclusion, and laxative documentation. failed_two_laxative_therapies attests to submitted dates of trial or inadequate response from at least two laxative therapies.",
    "Cautions (notes only): potential for gastrointestinal perforation; may cause severe or persistent diarrhea; monitor patients for symptoms of opioid withdrawal.",
    "Authorization (notes only): approval up to a maximum of 4 months.",
    "Quantity limits (notes only): 30-day supply at FDA approved dosage."
  ],
